A correction worth recording, because an earlier version of this file got it
wrong and the wrong version informed the task backlog.

This document declares `openapi: 3.1.0`, and that was assumed to be the first
blocker — rejected at a version gate before anything else could matter. There is
no version gate. paogen never inspects `$openApi->openapi` and never calls
`validate()`, so a 3.1 document is read structurally like any other.

More to the point, this document uses no 3.1 construct at all: no
`type: [T, "null"]`, no `const`, no `prefixItems`, no `unevaluatedProperties`.
It is a 3.0-shaped document carrying a 3.1 version string, which is why it
parses cleanly and reaches the emitters.

So the parser swap is not what stands between paogen and this client. Inline
payloads are, and they are the whole of it.
